At Sat, 08 Oct 2005 19:17:29 +0100,
Adrian McMenamin wrote:
> 
> Could someone let me know what this symbol is for? The documentation
> "how to write an ALSA driver" simply states: When the mmap is supported,
> add SNDRV_PCM_INFO_MMAP flag here
> 
> Now, I know MMAP will stand for memory mapped/mapping in some way, but
> could someone tell me what? Does this mean if the device is memory
> mapped, for instance? (I am not trying to write a PCI device driver and
> apologies for the basic nature of the question).

It means that the DMA buffers are memory-mapped to user-space so that
they can be accessed directly without read/write syscalls.


